Now I can see the issue clearly. Line 53-57:
```typescript
// Redirect if already authenticated
useEffect(() => {
  if (isAuthenticated) {
    navigate('/files');
  }
}, [isAuthenticated, navigate]);
```

This effect fires whenever `isAuthenticated` or `navigate` changes. When the login flow completes:
1. `setAccessToken` → `isAuthenticated: true` → Login re-renders → this effect fires → `navigate('/files')`
2. Test catches URL → navigates to `#/settings`
3. `setIsLoggingIn(false)` → Login re-renders (one more time) → if `navigate` identity changed → effect re-fires → `navigate('/files')` again!


The real problem is that when the route changes to `/settings`, the Login component's cleanup runs after the re-render from `setIsLoggingIn(false)`, so the effect can fire one more time before unmounting. I can fix this by checking if we're still on the login page before redirecting, or using `replace: true` to avoid the navigation race condition.

