With HashRouter, `location.pathname` is the path inside the hash. So when on `/#/settings`, `location.pathname === '/settings'`. The check `location.pathname === '/'` only triggers when on the root hash (`/#/`).


The Login component only renders when the route is `/`, so this effect wouldn't even run if the user is elsewhere. The SettingsPage must be redirecting back to `/` during enrollment, which would mount the Login component and trigger the wallet login chain that's showing up in the stack trace. The SettingsPage redirect effect checking for the `!isEnrolling` condition is likely what's causing this navigation.

Now I need to look more closely at the useMfa hook to see if `isEnrolling` might be flickering to false at some point during the enrollment process.

