Yes, confirmed. The redirect effect at line 57-61 checks `isAuthenticated && location.pathname === '/'` but does NOT check `isRequiredShare`. When context B gets the temp access token (which makes isAuthenticated=true), this effect fires and navigates to /files, unmounting the DeviceWaitingScreen before the approval request can be created.

The fix is straightforward: add `!isRequiredShare` to the condition:

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (isAuthenticated && !isRequiredShare && location.pathname === '/') {
    navigate('/files');
  }
}, [isAuthenticated, isRequiredShare, location.pathname, navigate]);


```

This ensures the redirect only fires when the user is fully authenticated (not in REQUIRED_SHARE state).

Applying the fix now...

